course: dictionary
lesson: 11913
title: Buried
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Buried comes from the verb bury, which means to put something into a hole in the ground and cover it with earth. The ending -ed shows that the action is finished, so something is hidden now. «The pirates buried their gold under a big tree.» The gold is under the ground, out of sight.
explain: Buried can also mean covered by lots of something, like sand, snow or papers. «The car was buried in snow after the storm.» You cannot see the car, because the snow is on top of it. Ask yourself: what is covering it? The snow is covering it, so buried means covered and hidden.
explain: Buried can mean deep inside something and hard to find. «The answer was buried in a long page of numbers.» The answer is there, but you have to search to find it. Try the swap check: put hidden in place of buried, and the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Bury is a verb: bury, buries, buried, burying. Buried is its past form.
fact: «Buried» means put into a hole in the ground and covered with earth, or put into a grave after death.
fact: «Buried» can also mean covered or hidden under lots of something, like sand, snow or papers.
fact: «Buried treasure» is treasure hidden in the ground, often by pirates.
fact: Archaeologists dig up buried things to learn about the past, and fossils are what is left of plants and animals buried in rock long ago.
exercise: «The pirates buried their gold on a little island.» What does buried mean here? | Left on a boat | *Put into a hole in the ground and covered with earth | Washed away by the sea | Painted bright gold
exercise: «The road was buried under deep snow all morning.» What does buried mean here? | Bright and shiny | *Covered and hidden under lots of something | Dug up and cleaned | Very tall
exercise: Ella says, «Seeds are buried in soil to grow.» Why are seeds buried? | *Hidden in soil so they can grow into plants | To keep them dry in the sun | Painted in bright colours | So they can fly away
test: «Archaeologists dug up the buried pots to learn about the past.» What does buried mean here? | Brand new | Carried to a museum | *Hidden in the ground for a long time | Broken into small pieces
test: Mia wrote, «The answer was buried deep in the book.» What does buried mean here? | *Deep inside and hard to find | Printed in big letters | Read out loud by a teacher | Written at the very start
exam: Which sentence uses buried to mean covered by lots of something? | «The pirates buried a chest on the beach.» | «The king was buried in a tomb.» | *«The desk was buried under a pile of unmarked papers.»
